            "review_title": "Review at Barbecue Garden",
            "review_text": "Kevin M\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam55 contributions\n0\nGreat Barbecued Beef with Cheese\nJul 2019 • Friends\nLast night we tried this restaurant, which has recently moved from its old location in D1. We were attracted by the special offer: the barbecued beef with cheese - 2 for the price of 1. It was fabulously tasty. I asked if it was Vietnamese or Australian beef, and was surprised to learn it was Vietnamese. It was the tenderest Vietnamese beef I have ever had. Two large platefuls were served, and we cooked it ourselves on the hotplate in the centre of our table. The beef had been marinated in spices and was delicious. I ate my beef with garlic fried rice and grilled aubergine. The bill for two of us was 320,000 - ridiculously cheap for such a large and wholesome meal.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 31, 2019",
